{% extends "template.njk" %}

{% set pageTitle = "Getting started with our APIs - HMCTS API Marketplace - GOV.UK" %}
{% set section = "get-started" %}
{% set breadcrumbs = [{ text: "Home", href: "/" }] %}

{% from "govuk/components/button/macro.njk" import govukButton %}

{% block content %}

<div class="govuk-grid-row">
  <div class="govuk-grid-column-two-thirds">

    <h1 class="govuk-heading-xl">Getting started with our APIs</h1>

    <p class="govuk-body-l">
      Learn about what APIs we offer and how you can connect to them.
    </p>

    <h2 class="govuk-heading-l" id="what-is-it">What is the HMCTS API Marketplace?</h2>

    <p class="govuk-body">
      The HMCTS API Marketplace is a central catalogue of data APIs from across His Majesty&rsquo;s
      Courts and Tribunals Service. Think of it as a library for data &mdash; teams can browse,
      understand, and request access to data feeds that power justice services.
    </p>

    <p class="govuk-body">
      The marketplace does not build or host the APIs itself. It makes them discoverable, documented,
      and accessible in one place &mdash; with governance controls to ensure only the right people can
      access the right data.
    </p>

    <h2 class="govuk-heading-l" id="steps">Steps to get connected</h2>

    <h3 class="govuk-heading-m">1. Read the consumer guidance</h3>

    <p class="govuk-body">
      Before you design your software, read the
      <a class="govuk-link" href="/documentation/consumer-guidance">consumer guidance</a>. It explains
      whether your organisation is eligible, how to use APIs responsibly, including rate limits,
      authentication and error handling, and the terms of use that apply to everyone using the
      marketplace.
    </p>

    <h3 class="govuk-heading-m" id="browse-the-catalogue">2. Browse the catalogue</h3>

    <p class="govuk-body">
      You do not need an account to browse the <a class="govuk-link" href="/api-catalogue">API
      catalogue</a>. You can see what each API returns and read the guidance, but you cannot call an API
      from the catalogue.
    </p>

    <h3 class="govuk-heading-m">3. Confirm your use case</h3>

    <p class="govuk-body">
      Before you go any further, confirm that you have a valid use case for the APIs you want to use.
      Production access is only approved for a valid use case, so be ready to explain yours when you
      apply.
    </p>

    <h3 class="govuk-heading-m" id="test-the-apis">4. Test the APIs - Try it now</h3>

    <p class="govuk-body">
      Try it now lets you test our APIs with dummy data before you ask for access to live data. You need
      a developer account to use it. It does not use live data.
    </p>

    <p class="govuk-body">
      To use Try it now:
    </p>

    <ol class="govuk-list govuk-list--number">
      <li><a class="govuk-link" href="/sign-in">Sign in</a>, or
        <a class="govuk-link" href="/sign-in">create a developer account</a> if you do not have one yet.
        You need an account to create an application for Try it now and test the APIs.</li>
      <li><a class="govuk-link" href="/account/applications/new">Create an application</a> for Try it now
        and add the APIs you want to test. Your Try it now credentials and keys are issued
        automatically, with no review.</li>
      <li>Test your software with the APIs.</li>
    </ol>

    <h3 class="govuk-heading-m">5. Apply for production access</h3>

    <p class="govuk-body">
      When you are ready to use live data, request production credentials for an application you have
      tested in Try it now.
    </p>

    <p class="govuk-body">
      Your production credentials request is reviewed by the HMCTS Data Access Team, and you will get
      an outcome within 5 working days of submitting it. This is currently an offline process, so look
      out for emails requesting clarification, or confirming approval or rejection.
    </p>

    <p class="govuk-body">
      If your request is approved, the API Marketplace team will issue your production credentials and
      keys. You can then use them to call our APIs with live data.
    </p>

    <h2 class="govuk-heading-l" id="help">Get help and support</h2>

    <p class="govuk-body">
      If you have any issues, either during development or once your software is live, you can
      contact the marketplace team at <a class="govuk-link" href="mailto:APIMarketplace@hmcts.net">APIMarketplace@hmcts.net</a>.
    </p>

    <p class="govuk-body">
      Read the <a class="govuk-link" href="/documentation/consumer-guidance">consumer guidance</a> for
      detailed information on using APIs responsibly and on your legal obligations.
    </p>

    {{ govukButton({
      text: "Browse the API catalogue",
      href: "/api-catalogue",
      isStartButton: true
    }) }}

  </div>
</div>

{% endblock %}
